                                "sense_id": "ed1d3b2d-0288-357d-94ad-0ba2655c0a84",
                                "text": "I then glanced round the room; and besides the bedstead and centre table, could see no other furniture belonging to the place, but a rude shelf, the four walls, and a papered fireboard representing a man striking a whale."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "22339335-056c-4fbe-af86-2780dcf1da30",
                                "sense_id": "ed1d3b2d-0288-357d-94ad-0ba2655c0a84",
                                "text": "1915, Mary E. Wilkins Freeman, Emancipation\nA stovepipe had been fitted into an iron fireboard covering the great fireplace"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fb025933-0a4a-43c6-b870-6112b717cff2",
                                "sense_id": "ed1d3b2d-0288-357d-94ad-0ba2655c0a84",
                                "text": "The wind whopped and spat into the chimney; and now and then a puff of wood-smoke blew out and mounted up along the blackened fireboard."
